{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"masonic-excusable-guppy","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe 48 `exact`/`co_names` MCP tools are hand-copied closures (`src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`, `_mcp_writes.py`) whose only guard is a 572-LOC introspection script (`scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py`), a 486-LOC test and a 919-line manifest that compare names. The epic's experiment found three undeclared shape divergences it cannot see (`list_tickets.priority`, `bridge_run.profile`, `transition_ticket` parameter order). Ticket topaz-blubbery-mice (c996-8a5f-5123-4f8e) chose \"no generated adapters (Pattern A)\" for all three surfaces; the post-oracle escape lowly-lawrencium-ovenbird shows the MCP copy still drifts. ADR 0118 supersedes that clause for MCP only; the CLI stays under ADR 0100. Cites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n## Approach\nNew `src/rebar/_mcp_derive.py` (factory plus hooks, about 250 LOC) and `src/rebar/_mcp_tool_specs.py` (the override table, about 500 LOC). `ToolSpec` is a frozen dataclass: `name, library, registrar (\"read\"|\"write\"|\"bridge_mutation\"), annotation (preset key), description (verbatim, including the current 8-space continuation indentation so bytes are identical), strip (extra params), params (per-param annotation and default overrides), order, pins (fixed kwargs; callables evaluated per call), pre (gate hooks), post (result hooks), schema (kind plus name, reused by `_mcp_schema`)`. The factory `derive_tool(mcp, spec, ctx)` resolves hints with `typing.get_type_hints(fn, globalns=vars(sys.modules[fn.__module__]), localns=vars(rebar.types))` (never `inspect.signature(eval_str=True)`, which raises on the `TYPE_CHECKING`-only TypedDict names); builds an `inspect.Signature` from the library parameters minus `repo_root`, `_`-prefixed names and `spec.strip`, applying `params`/`order` (VAR_POSITIONAL becomes `list[T]`); creates ONE wrapper `def tool(*args, **kwargs)` that `sig.bind`s, runs the PRE hooks, calls `getattr(rebar, spec.library)(**bound, **pins)`, runs the POST hooks in order, and sets `__name__`, `__doc__`, `__signature__`, `__annotations__`; then registers with `mcp.tool(annotations=presets[spec.annotation])(tool)`. Because `mcp.tool` is the already-layered decorator, the four existing layers attach unchanged: error guard (`_mcp_errors.py:88-138`), JS-safe guard (`:223-259`), advisory suppression (`_lib_warn.py:67-107`), operation snapshot (`_operation_config.py:313-357`), composed in `mcp_server.py:606-632`; `functools.wraps` propagates `__signature__` through them. The named hooks, pins, the eight input overrides, and the ten declared divergences carried verbatim from the manifest are itemised in this ticket's first comment. Registration-time gating is unchanged: `register_write_tools` still returns early when `ctx.readonly()` (`_mcp_writes.py:172`) and `register_bridge_tools` registers the four bridge mutations only when not read-only (`_mcp_reads.py:164`); the 16 `mcp_only` tools remain hand-written in their registrars, so `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py` grouping and output are unchanged; `_mcp_inflight` and `_cap_workflow_payload` are consumed only by `mcp_only` tools (`_mcp_llm.py:23`, `get_workflow_*`) and stay where they are. Delete the parity script, its test, the manifest, `Makefile:298-310`, the stub at `tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py:324-326`, and the manifest row at `docs/generated-artifacts.md:39` (adding the golden's row). Write `docs/adr/0118-mcp-surface-derived-from-library.md` (text in the second comment) with `docs/adr/.numbers/0118`, index it in `docs/adr/README.md`, and describe the derivation and override table in `docs/architecture.md`'s MCP section.\n\n## Scope\nNew: `src/rebar/_mcp_derive.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_tool_specs.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_tool_surface_golden.py`, `docs/adr/0118-mcp-surface-derived-from-library.md`, `docs/adr/.numbers/0118`. Delete: `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py`, `tests/unit/test_mcp_library_parity.py`, `tests/unit/mcp_library_parity_manifest.json`. Edit: `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_schema.py` (its table reads `spec.schema`), `Makefile`, `tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py`, `docs/generated-artifacts.md`, `docs/adr/README.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`. Kept unchanged: `tests/interfaces/facades/test_parity.py`, `tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py`, `write_parity_contract.py`, `adapters.py`, `.github/complexity-baseline.json` (`register_read_tools`/`register_write_tools` lose nested defs and bucket `stale`, which passes). Out of scope: the 16 MCP-only tools, the CLI, the library signatures.\n\n## Testing\nGolden capture, run once from the schema story's landed tree before writing any derivation code, with the SHA recorded in the test docstring (command in the first comment) producing `tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json` with `inputSchema`, `description`, and `annotations` for all 64 tools. `test_mcp_tool_surface_golden.py`: `test_live_surface_equals_golden` parametrized over the 64 golden names (dict comparison; `required` lists compared as lists); `test_golden_covers_exactly_the_live_tools` (set equality both ways); `test_every_derived_tool_names_a_public_library_symbol` (each spec's `library` is in `rebar.__all__`); `test_stripped_params_are_only_repo_root_private_or_declared` (a spec may strip only `repo_root`, `_*`, or a name listed in its `divergence` note). Behavioural suites pass unchanged: `tests/interfaces/facades/test_parity.py`, `tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py`, `tests/unit/test_cross_session_mcp.py`, `test_mcp_writes.py`, `test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py`, `test_mcp_output_schema_canonical.py`. `python scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py --check`, `python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py`, `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] For all 64 tools, `list_tools()` `inputSchema`, `description`, and `annotations` equal the committed golden (the golden test).\n- [ ] `_mcp_reads.py` and `_mcp_writes.py` contain `def` bodies only for the 16 `mcp_only` tools plus registrars and helpers; `grep -c \"@mcp.tool\" src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py` reports 8 and 1.\n- [ ] `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py`, `tests/unit/test_mcp_library_parity.py`, and the manifest are gone and `make lint` no longer invokes the script (grep and `make -n lint`).\n- [ ] The behavioural parity suites named above pass without modification (`git diff --stat` on those paths is empty).\n- [ ] `docs/mcp-reference.md` is unchanged (`--check`); ADR 0118 passes `check_adr_numbers.py` and is indexed (CI).\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0; the complexity ratchet reports only `stale`; the mechanism ratchet reports `new=0` after `--update-stale` for the removed `scripts/check_*.py` gate.","id":"c296-4bc7-26be-489d","parent_id":"04f1-5f92-3119-4731","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Derive the 48 library-backed MCP tools from the annotated signatures through one factory and an override table; delete the name-only parity gate; write ADR 0118"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788806907265178664,"uuid":"baecbe42-d857-4eb6-a4b5-821f6ab443ed"}